Provenance of the files in proxy/
=================================

This directory mixes code written for Claudefuscator with a vendored copy
of a separate project, "local-ai-proxy", by the same author and under the
same licence. Both are MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Rafael Vuijk, so the root
LICENSE covers everything here.

This file exists anyway, because "same author, same licence" is the kind of
fact that is obvious to the person who knows it and invisible to everyone
else. Vendored code with no licence header invites exactly one question,
and answering it in advance is cheaper than answering it repeatedly.

CLAUDEFUSCATOR'S OWN FILES

    claudefuscator_core.py      hand-port of the canonical tokenizer
    veil.py                     scrub outbound, restore inbound
    config_merge.py             mirror of shared/config-merge.js
    start-proxy.ps1
    tests/test_parity.py        asserts the port matches the vectors
    tests/test_veil.py
    tests/test_merge_parity.py

VENDORED FROM local-ai-proxy

    detect.py  sse.py  local_request.py
    rules.toml  test_rules.toml
    start-claude.ps1
    __init__.py  tests/__init__.py  tests/conftest.py
    tests/test_detect.py  tests/test_local_request.py  tests/test_sse.py

VENDORED AND THEN MODIFIED HERE

    lite_llm_proxy.py           upstream, with the veil hooks added by
                                tools/patch-proxy.py
    tests/test_proxy_integration.py

Keeping the split visible matters for a practical reason rather than a
legal one: `tools/patch-proxy.py` reapplies the hooks, so a file in the
vendored list can be replaced wholesale from upstream, and a file in the
first list cannot.

WHY THIS DIRECTORY IS STILL HERE

Proxy mode is no longer the recommended path — see PROXY-NOTES.md — but it
remains the only way to measure what another mode actually emitted, which
is how mod mode was verified. Deleting it would remove the only instrument
that can audit the thing most people will rely on.
